# Enforce CRLF line endings for markdown files to eliminate git status noise on Windows/WSL environments
*.md text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts and git hooks MUST stay LF. With core.autocrlf=true git would
# otherwise check them out CRLF, and git executes hooks DIRECTLY via their shebang --
# where a trailing CR yields `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`. The hook then does not run
# at all, which is precisely how a guard becomes silently absent (AGENTS 5.5.1: a
# fallback that quietly returns success is a latent incident). Invoking the same file
# as `sh <file>` happens to tolerate the CRs, so this does NOT reproduce in casual
# testing -- it only bites on the real execution path, on someone else's clone.
scripts/hooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
